  16 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[6;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[7;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m18 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[7;7H (B[m[38:2:158:206:106mCURR_SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"[8;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m19 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[8;7H (B[m[38:2:158:206:106msource "$CURR_SCRIPT_DIR/../etc/naledi.conf"[9;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m21 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[9;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mInitially, I used the echo command and redirected the output using (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m>(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m to[5C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mthe created shell script. However, the variable calls in those two lines[4C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mwould be written into that file after being expanded out, meaning the path[C[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mto (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m would be written as is in the new file, resulting in a        (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoded(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m path, which is what we want to avoid.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  22 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[14;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  23 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[15;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried escaping the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m$(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m for each variable with (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m\(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m,  it did not work, I in  [K[3C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mfact got syntax error because of my bad placement of those but even when I   (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mdid place them correctly, it did not work. I also tried placing the variable (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mcalls in single quotes, that did not help either.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  24 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[19;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  25 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[20;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWhat eventually did work was using (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mprintf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m with the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m%s(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m option,  and with    [K[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mthat I was able to preserve and write those two lines as is.[K
