(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  10   (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mAnother automation script I had tried is one that I use to run shell scripts and shell commands whose tasks require the banner to be shown in running the output.    (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::224:175:104m[38:2:192:202:245mits(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m aim is to avoid having to invoke my banner function each time it is needed to be run when running a shell script or shell command needing it. I aliased it "(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mmyrun(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m" (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245min "~/.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mbashrc(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m"[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  11   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  12   (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried making a shell script to automate seeding my data files. I wanted to be able to whenever necessary, be able to quickly re-seed the needed data files.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  13   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  14   (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### Failures and Problems(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  15   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWith the feature to be able to create scripts already having the shebang statement, and (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m import without (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m itself was       (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mproblematic. Firstly to import (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m without (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to it,  after the shebang statement, I placed the following:(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m-(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  16   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  18   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106mCURR_SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  19   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106msource "$CURR_SCRIPT_DIR/../etc/naledi.conf"(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  21   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mInitially, I used the echo command and redirected the output using (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m>(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m to the created shell script. However, the variable calls in those two lines would be written    [K[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245minto that file after being expanded out, meaning the path to (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m would be written as is in the new file, resulting in a (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoded(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m path, which is what we want  (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mto avoid.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  22   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  23   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried escaping the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m$(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m for each variable with (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m\(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m,  it did not work, I in fact got syntax error because of my bad placement of those but even when I did place them  [K[3C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mcorrectly, it did not work. I also tried placing the variable calls in single quotes, that did not help either.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  24   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  25   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWhat eventually did work was using (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mprintf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m with the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m%s(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m option,  and with that I was able to preserve and write those two lines as is.[K
