_SCRIPT_DIR/../lib/validate_(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconfig(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.sh"[80X[25;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m121   [26;3H122   (B[m[4:3m[58:2::224:175:104m[38:2:192:202:245mvalidate(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m_(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconfig(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[7X[27;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m123   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245msource "$(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mCURR(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m_SCRIPT_DIR/../etc/(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m"[120X[28;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m125   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106mwith `validate_config` being more comprehensive.(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[9X[29;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m126   [30;3H127   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106m### What I accomplished(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[135X[31;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m128   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106m- I managed to complete and meet all my goals for the validation shell script for `naledi.conf`.[32;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m129   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[14X[33;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m130   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106m- I also successfully replaced legacy code that initially only checked if `naledi.conf` existed in all the shell scripts that were created before `validate_config.   (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m        (B[m[38:2:158:206:106msh` with just one function call `validate_config` after importing the `validate_config.sh` shell script.[35;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m131   [36;3H132   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106m- most importantly, I successfully changed the logic in my `create_script.sh` module utilized by `mytouch` to make sure it now adds the new method of validating      (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m        (B[m[38:2:158:206:106m`naledi.conf` and required operating parameters.(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m-[38;3H(B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m133 (B[0;1m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[38;8H [?2026l[?2026h[4A(